  "summary": "Completed the final Apply evidence gate for RFC-0002 S-04. Both formatting checks and clean dependency-order compilation pass. The repository matrix passes 913 tests: 601 quantities, 13 reference data, 9 application, 18 runtime, 13 instrument economics, 40 risk, 7 order model, 16 execution scenario, 38 fee policy and downstream integration, and 158 completed-JAR/compiler/adversarial tests. JMH compilation passes. The fee-policy JAR contains 132 entries and 90 canonical classes with no provisional package, retired capability, or reverse class entry; public javap and production scans confirm pure explicit inputs, no effects, no source-market attachment, no identity reconciliation, no unlawful monoid, and no raw-scalar PnL kernel. Strict OpenSpec validation, all eleven deterministic Corgi readiness checks, and the read-only cross-artifact semantic review pass at planning revision sha256:b2226bdaf8f713cf48bb49f599da6b5cd84462cb96d8f028a6263caed76c4158 with no drift. Automated Task Group review covered exact Run/Group identity, AC-013 through AC-016 evidence, validation, package/source audits, architecture, performance/security applicability, checkpoint integrity, and gate separation with no findings; its final checkpoint changed no file, triaged no finding, and is not canonical whole-change Verify or Human Review. The checkpoint transitions only to awaiting_verify and does not begin boundary codecs or later lifecycle gates."
